Original commit body from 41517db9c064a50fcb92c1738eafec1f2613c381:

Owner decision (2026-10-06), recorded in place per the ADR lifecycle rules:
parsing the source of installed dependencies (Mix deps/, node_modules/,
venv site-packages, package-manager vendor/, Pods/, ...) is off by default,
recognised by content (generalising the virtualenv rule), disclosed when
skipped, and opted into per package with a planned --trace-deps.

- ADR-0004: new section "Installed dependency source" (third answer to
  "why was this file skipped?"); corrects the false claim that symbol
  extraction runs only on tiers 1-2 (a Mix fixture yields tier-3 deps/
  symbols and a resolved call into them); rewrites the "additions only"
  banner and the matching Consequences line.
- ADR-0016 §7: "trace everything" becomes "trace only when opted in;
  otherwise a call into dependency source is untraced, I/O unknown,
  never clean"; Context sentence points at the rule.
- Spec: §14 Motivation and default behaviour, the stale --exclude
  default list (venv/ is not a default exclude), --trace-deps marked
  planned, installed_deps_skipped planned, §15 symbol-extraction row.

Implementation tracked by WI-bapal and WI-pogar; nothing here ships
behaviour. Closes WI-mogit.

